      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Chronic pain syndromes such as fibromyalgia and reflex sympathetic dystrophy constitute an increasing percentage of new patient referrals to pediatric rheumatology clinics. It is surprising then that so few studies have been published on these syndromes. This review focuses on the investigations that are central to our understanding of this difficult diagnostic area."},
